#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_intersecting

#% text
# `is_intersecting(xs, ys)` is `true` when the lists `xs` and `ys` have at least one element in common.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Elements are compared by identity: `1` and `1.0` differ.

#% item
# `is_disjoint` is the opposite.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_intersecting([1, 2], [2, 3])
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_intersecting([a, b], [c])
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_disjoint`, `intersection`
